const IMPROVELOG = "ts and the anomaly audit\nare all clean, and the one new QQQ data point - while part of an emerging 3-high lag pattern -\nis a single session, not yet the sustained, confirmed pattern the discipline requires before\ntouching prediction code; it goes on the watch list instead. `forecast_ledger.json` is still slowly\ngrowing (now ~34.3 MB), not yet a real problem. Honesty features (hit-rate displays, random-control\ncomparisons, grading, coherence gate) and `tickers.txt` are untouched.\n\n**Watch next:** whether the QQQ-high lag (actual high printing well before the predicted date)\nrepeats a 4th time, which would clear the bar for a method-weighting fix; whether HOOD's spread\nrecovers above the $99.95 breakeven in its final 4 trading days or settles into a realized ~$1,185\nloss at the 10/30 expiry; whether META's slide below its $660 long strike continues or reverses with\nfour weeks still on the clock; the slow growth of `forecast_ledger.json`; and the standing list -\nNVDA's small-sample hit rate, the GOOGL-highs/AMZN-lows naive-baseline gaps, HOOD's calibration\nceiling, and whether SPY/VOO/META/SPCX ever produce a confirmed swing to grade.\n\n## 2026-10-28 (Wed) \u2014 HOOD's open spread locks in near-certain max loss with 2 days left; grade + log only\n\n**Today's data situation:** this sandbox's own `fetch_data.py` was blocked again before reaching\nYahoo - all 12 tickers failed with a proxy-level connection refusal (confirmed via the proxy's own\nstatus log: \"gateway answered 403 to CONNECT,\" a policy block on this sandbox, not a Yahoo-side\nblock). No raw per-ticker CSVs exist locally (gitignored, never recreated here), so `analyze.py`\ncorrectly refused to run against the missing files and raised its own safety error rather than\nrisk publishing an empty or broken build - exactly the behavior that safeguard is there for. The\nlive dashboard is instead running on the separate scheduled GitHub Actions refresh's own build,\ngenerated today at 5:42 PM ET with the last daily bar dated 2026-10-28 - today's real session did\nland. Ran the coherence check (passes clean, 12/12 tickers), the full test suite (all 13\n`test_*.py` files, every test passing) and the anomaly audit against that build: everything is\nclean, zero anomalies.\n\n**Grades reviewed:** TSLA n=13 (31%/38%), QQQ n=65 (23%/28%), JPM n=29 (14%/21%), GOOGL n=45\n(20%/22%), NVDA n=19 (11%/16%), GC=F n=22 (18%/18%) - all byte-for-byte unchanged from Monday, no\nnew resolutions. HOOD moved to n=67 (16%/24%, was 64 at 17%/25%): three more HOOD predictions\nresolved, all as full misses (the predicted window closed with no matching high or low ever\nconfirmed), nudging its already-weak hit rate down a point - consistent with the long-standing,\nalready-logged HOOD calibration problem, not a new issue. AMZN, SPY, VOO, META and SPCX remain at\nn=0, the same ongoing condition. The two open real spreads both got worse again: HOOD (trade 8,\nsold $101 put / bought $96 put x3, expires 10/30) is now priced with HOOD at $90.10 - well below\neven the $96 long strike, with only 2 trading days left (10/29-10/30) and effectively no path left\nto avoid the ~$1,185 max loss. META (trade 9, sold $670 put / bought $660 put x2, expires 11/20) is\nnow priced with META at $618.00 (down from $633.00 on Monday), also below its $660 long strike,\nthough it still has about three weeks of runway to recover before the max $1,500 loss would lock\nin. The owner's journal also shows two new pending (unfilled) GTC orders placed today - a HOOD\n88/83 put spread (#74, replacing the voided #67) and a TSLA 412.5/422.5 call spread (#75) - neither\nhas filled yet, so neither changes any open position.\n\n**What changed and why:** no dashboard logic change today. Coherence, the full test suite and the\nanomaly audit are all clean, and nothing crossed the 3+-graded-day pattern bar: HOOD's dip is a\ncontinuation of its already-tracked calibration weakness, not a new signal, and the QQQ-high lag\nflagged Monday did not get a 4th data point today (count unchanged at n=65). `forecast_ledger.json`\ncontinues its slow growth (now ~38.4 MB, up from ~34.3 MB two days ago) - still not breaking\nanything, but the growth rate itself is worth a closer look soon if it keeps climbing this fast.\nHonesty features (hit-rate displays, random-control comparisons, grading, coherence gate) and\n`tickers.txt` are untouched.\n\n**Watch next:** whether HOOD's spread closes Friday 10/30 at its ~$1,185 max loss (no realistic\nrecovery path with 2 trading days and HOOD $6+ below the long strike) - this would be its first\nfully realized loss on a graded real position; whether META's slide below its $660 long strike\ncontinues or reverses with about three weeks still on the clock; whether either of today's two new\npending orders (#74 HOOD, #75 TSLA) actually fills; the accelerating growth of\n`forecast_ledger.json`; whether the QQQ-high lag repeats a 4th time; and the standing list - NVDA's\nsmall-sample hit rate, the GOOGL-highs/AMZN-lows naive-baseline gaps, HOOD's calibration ceiling,\nand whether SPY/VOO/META/SPCX ever produce a confirmed swing to grade.\n\n## 2026-10-29 (Thu) \u2014 JPM's grading catches up in one big batch; HOOD's spread rolls into tomorrow's expiry at a locked-in loss; grade + log only\n\n**Today's data situation:** this sandbox's own `fetch_data.py` was blocked again - all 12\ntickers failed with the same proxy-level 403 seen on recent days (confirmed via the proxy's\nstatus log: \"gateway answered 403 to CONNECT\" on Yahoo's finance API, a policy block on this\nsandbox, not a Yahoo-side block). With no raw per-ticker CSVs available, `analyze.py` correctly\nrefused to run and raised its own safety error rather than risk publishing a broken build. The\nlive dashboard is instead running on the separate scheduled GitHub Actions refresh's own build,\nlast updated today at 5:41 PM ET with the daily bar dated 2026-10-29 - today's real session did\nland there. Ran the coherence check (passes clean, 12/12 tickers), the full test suite (138\ntests, all passing) and the anomaly audit against that build: everything is clean, zero\nanomalies.\n\n**Grades reviewed:** the standout change is JPM, which jumped from n=29 (14%/21%) on Monday's\nreview to n=62 (8%/13%) today - 33 more predictions resolved in a single cycle, and skewed\nheavily toward misses. This is not new data corruption: the grading code only resolves a\nprediction once its target date is 8+ trading days old *and* a matching swing has actually been\nconfirmed in the price action, so a steady, mostly one-directional grind in JPM (it has climbed\nfrom about $332 to $345 over the last two weeks without a sizable pullback) lets a long backlog\nof old low-side calls get confirmed - and judged - all at once rather than a few per day. The\nmechanism checks out and every safety gate is clean, so this is logged as a one-time catch-up,\nnot a bug, but the post-catch-up hit rate (8%/13%) is now JPM's grading baseline and is worth\nwatching over the next few sessions to see if it holds or recovers. Smaller, ordinary moves\nelsewhere: QQQ n=65\u219266 (23%/27%, basically flat), GOOGL n=45\u219247 (20%/21%, basically flat). TSLA\n(13, 31%/38%), HOOD (67, 16%/24%), NVDA (19, 11%/16%) and GC=F (22, 18%/18%) are all unchanged\nsince Wednesday. AMZN, SPY, VOO, META and SPCX remain at n=0.\n\n**Open real positions:** HOOD's put credit spread (trade 8, sold $101 / bought $96, x3) expires\n**tomorrow, Fri 10/30**, and HOOD has kept falling - now $88.00, a full $8 below even the $96 long\nstrike, with zero trading time left to recover. This is effectively certain to close at its full\n~$1,185 max loss tomorrow. META's spread (trade 9, sold $670 / bought $660, x2, expires 11/20) also\nkept sliding, now $619.85 (down from $618.00 Wednesday and $633.00 Monday) - about $40 below its\n$660 long strike, with roughly three weeks still on the clock to recover before the $1,500 max\nloss would lock in.\n\n**What changed and why:** no dashboard logic change today. Coherence, the full test suite and the\nanomaly audit are all clean, and the JPM jump - while large - is a one-time grading catch-up\nexplained by the code's own confirmation-delay design, not a 3+-day pattern or a demonstrated bug,\nso it does not meet the bar for a code change. `forecast_ledger.json` is at 37.9 MB, essentially\nflat versus the ~38.4 MB logged Wednesday. Honesty features (hit-rate displays, random-control\ncomparisons, grading, coherence gate) and `tickers.txt` are untouched.\n\n**Watch next:** whether HOOD's spread actually closes Friday 10/30 at its ~$1,185 max loss (no\nrealistic recovery path remains); whether META's slide below its $660 long strike continues or\nreverses with about three weeks still on the clock; whether JPM's post-catch-up 8%/13% hit rate\nholds, recovers, or keeps sliding over the next few graded days; whether today's pending GTC order\n(#76 TSLA 415/425C) fills; and the standing list - NVDA's small-sample hit rate, HOOD's calibration\nceiling, and whether SPY/VOO/META/SPCX ever produce a confirmed swing to grade.\n";
